---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Our story" description="Diapontia comes from one family olive grove in north-west Corfu, facing the Diapontian islands.">
  <article class="narrow">
    <p class="eyebrow">Our story</p>
    <h1>A family grove facing the Diapontian islands</h1>
    <!-- TODO: Yiannis, replace the bracketed parts with your family's real details. -->
    <p class="lead">
      Off the north-west coast of Corfu lie three small islands: Othonoi, Ereikoussa and Mathraki.
      Together they are the Diapontian islands. Our family's olive grove looks out at them.
    </p>
    <p>
      The trees in the grove are hundreds of years old. [Who planted them, or how long the family has
      tended them.] Each winter the family picks the olives and takes them to be pressed.
    </p>
    <p>
      For most of that time the oil never left the island. It went on our table, to neighbours and to
      relatives. Diapontia is the first time we have bottled it to sell, starting with a small batch of
      100 bottles for the UK.
    </p>

    <h2>How we make sure it is extra virgin</h2>
    <p>
      "Extra virgin" is a legal grade, not a description. An independent laboratory tests every batch
      before it is bottled. Only oil that meets the extra virgin standard carries the Diapontia name.
    </p>

    <h2>Bottled in Greece, sent from the UK</h2>
    <p>
      A bottler in Greece fills and labels each 750 ml bottle. The bottles travel to the UK, where we
      store them somewhere cool and dark and pack every order by hand.
    </p>

    <h2>Our logo</h2>
    <p>
      The mark on every bottle is an olive tree with Othonoi and Diaplo drawn beneath it, as we see them from
      the grove.
    </p>

    <p><a class="btn btn-primary" style="display:inline-flex" href="/">Buy a bottle</a></p>
  </article>
</Base>
